ck" content="true" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:android:url" content="meetup://" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:ios:url" content="meetup://" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:web:url" content="https://www.meetup.com/" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:site" content="@meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:image" content="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/shared/meetup-flyer.png" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:description" content="Find Meetup events and groups so you can do more of what matters to you and meet people near you who share your interests." data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:iphone" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:iphone" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:ipad" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:ipad" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:googleplay" content="com.meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:googleplay" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow" data-next-head=""/><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.meetup.com/find/" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" data-next-head=""/><script type="application/ld+json" data-next-head="">[{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"One Last Backcountry Weekend in Frontenac","url":"https://www.meetup.com/wildernessunion/events/316360750/","description":"**Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our website.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/weekend-in-frontenac)**\n\n**Fall (aka shoulder season) camping brings the serene beauty of the backcountry, without the crowds and bugs.**\n\nAt this time of year, Frontenac will be less busy and the trail into Big Clear Lake belongs mostly to us. It's a 9km hike to reach the site, working through root tangled trails and stretches of open granite typical of this stretch of the Canadian Shield. Only the most stubborn leaves will remain on the trees and you’ll enjoy long sightlines through bare branches where the canopy used to be. The pace is steady and moderate the whole way in, never technical but never quite letting up either.\n\nWe set up camp on the shore of Big Clear Lake as the light starts to drop, we get a fire going, and cook dinner together. Late October nights out here are serene, with a sky full of stars over the lake.\n\nIn the morning, we’ll take our time over breakfast before packing up and heading out along the other side of Big Salmon Lake: a different stretch of trail from the one we hiked in on, with its own look at the park before we're back where we started.\n\nBy the time we're back at the cars, you'll have had that sweet final night of the year in the backcountry.\n\nWhat's included\n\n* Professional & certified guides\n* ‍All camp meals, cooking equipment and mess kits\n* ‍Tents\n\nSleeping bags and sleep pads can be rented from WU for a small fee.\n\n**Accessibility**\nWilderness Union is committed to making our adventures as accessible as possible. If you wish to make an accommodation request relating to a disability or provide feedback, please do so by sending an email to info@wildernessunion.com\n\n**Highlights**\n**Last Trip of the Season:** The final overnight on the calendar before WU's backcountry program pauses for winter\n**Shoulder Season Solitude**: Long, quiet stretches of trail, with the lake mostly to yourselves.\n**A Clear Night Sky:** Bare branches and dry autumn air make for some of the best stargazing conditions of the year at the campsite.\n\n**Event cost: $265+HST. $70 optional transport also available. Please register [here.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/weekend-in-frontenac)**\n\n**About Wilderness Union**\nWilderness Union is deliberate about building an outdoors community that connects you to the life-changing magic of the outdoors and helps you find your people.\n\nMembers range from 20-40 years old. The group is a mix of GTA locals and newcomers to Toronto from within Canada and abroad.\n\nAttendance numbers on Meetup don't reflect our actual event attendance - we typically have 15-20 community members at each event. Large enough that there's someone new to meet but small enough that it's not overwhelming!\n\n***Learn more at our website [www.wildernessunion.com](https://www.wildernessunion.com/)***","startDate":"2026-10-24T10:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Toronto","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":", Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/wildernessunion/"},"performer":"Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"کارگاه آموزش درآمد زایی با مهارت General Mounting ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/iranian-job-seekers/events/316494446/","description":"سلام خدمت همه دوستان\nعزیزانی که مایلند در کارگاه آموزشی یک روزه یادگیری مهارت های General Mounting و آشنایی و درآمد زایی با اپلیکیشن Taskrabbit شرکت کنند حتما در این پست اعلام کنند تا لینک گروه براشون ارسال شود. 🙏","startDate":"2026-10-24T13:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Downtown Toronto","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Downtown, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Iranian Job seekers 😉","url":"https://www.meetup.com/iranian-job-seekers/"},"performer":"Iranian Job seekers 😉"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"All-Level &Beginner Friendly $10 Drop In Saturday Morning @ CA Badminton ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ca-badminton-meetup-toronto-group-gta/events/316332816/","description":":Saturday Morning Drop In\nCost $ 10 \\*\\*\\*\n\\* Included Plastic birdies, please try to have cash and pay before playing.\n\\*\\*\\*(Cash Only) (Cash Only) (Cash Only)\n\nLocation: 1370 Birchmount Rd, Unit 6\n\\*The close intersection in Birchmount Rd & Lawrence Ave.\nTime: Saturday 9:30 AM - 12 PM\n\\*\\*\\*9:30 AM- 12 PM 3 courts available\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\\*Please bring your own racquet,\n\\*Please bring indoor gym sport shoes. (Change shoes in the club)\n\\*\\*\\*\n\\*This weekly gathering is for all levels (beginner to advance) badminton players.\n\\*No outside food allowed.\n\\* This event is for the purpose of playing friendly double games and for all levels of players from beginner to advance. Please do not use this as an opportunity to do training and singles games.\nAttendance in effect -please give at least 24hr notice in advance for cancelation so others may have time to react. Late show and no-shows maybe permanently removed from group and unable to rejoin.\n\\*Only registered members can participate; visitors are not permitted. If you wish to participate, please register as a member first, and then view the event details and participation instructions.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* ⚠️⚠️⚠️\nTo ensure efficient use of event slots and fairness, all registered participants must confirm their attendance with the group administrator before the specified deadline (if a waitlist exists). \\* Before the deadline, registered members have the right to cancel and priority. To ensure fairness, if no response is received after the deadline, the waiting list member has priority.\n\nIf you do not confirm your attendance within 72 hours before the event, or are absent, your slot may be reassigned to a waiting list candidate or a new member. This rule aims to ensure fairness and maximize the participation opportunities for all members. Since the venue cost is shared by all confirmed participants, 🛎️ those who do not attend must notify the administrator before the deadline. Failure to notify the administrator before the deadline will result in payment of the venue cost. Thank you for your understanding. \\*Please note: Failure to pay the venue cost will result in your cancellation of membership.\n\nSlot allocation is based on the order of candidate responses. To ensure fairness and better coordination, when a registered candidate cancels their slot, the administrator will send a separate notification to all candidates each time slots open. Due to limited availability, places will be allocated on a first-come, first-served basis based on response time.\n\n\\*If you need to cancel your participation, please notify the administrator at least 24 hours before the event. Late cancellations will incur venue fees. Thank you for your understanding and cooperation.\n\n\\*To ensure fairness and transparency, each participant needs to confirm individually. Members who fail to cancel their registration and complete payment within the specified time will be permanently disqualified.\n\nPlease note that if you confirm participation on behalf of another member, you will be responsible for that member's event costs.\n\nTo maintain fairness for all participants, please inform your friends that they must also confirm.\n\n\\*In the event of repeated violations, the administrator reserves the right to make the final decision.\n\nThank you for your understanding and cooperation.\n\n* After reading the event details, members can contact the administrator via message.","startDate":"2026-10-24T13:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"CA Badminton Academy","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Scarborough","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1370 Birchmount rd, unit 6, Scarborough, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"CA Badminton Meetup Toronto Group GTA","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ca-badminton-meetup-toronto-group-gta/"},"performer":"CA Badminton Meetup Toronto Group GTA"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🍂 Fall Walk: Rouge National Urban Park and  Picnic🌳","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/316183314/","description":"# 🍂🌳 Fall Walk: Rouge National Urban Park 🌳🍁\n\n### A Real Hike, Beautiful Fall Colours & a Picnic Together\n\nWant to get out of the city without actually leaving Toronto?\n\n**Rouge National Urban Park** is Canada's only urban national park — and one of the most popular hikes we do.\nOnce you get onto the trail, it can be hard to believe you're still in Toronto. Forest paths, rolling hills, changing leaves, and quiet stretches of wilderness make this feel much more like a trip outside the city than a walk through it.\nAnd fall is one of the best times to experience it.\n\nThis is **a real hike**, though. There are some hills and ups and downs, so it isn't the best choice if you're looking for an easy, flat walk.\nBut if you're up for the challenge, there's something satisfying about reaching the end knowing you did it together.\nAnd then we'll have a picnic. 🧺\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🥾 What We'll Do\n\nWe'll meet at **Don Mills Station** and take the 85C bus together toward Rouge National Urban Park.\nOnce we arrive, we'll begin our hike through the park.\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Hike through forest and open spaces 🌳\n* Enjoy the fall colours 🍂\n* Navigate the hills and changing terrain\n* Take in some beautiful views\n* Stop for a short break along the route\n* Finish at the Park's Welcome Centre\n* Have a **30–40 minute group picnic** afterward 🧺\n\nThe hike takes approximately **2½ hours**, plus a short break.\nAfterward, we'll take some time to relax, eat, and enjoy each other's company.\n\n***\n\n## 🍁 Fall Weather & Expectations\n\nThis is a **moderately challenging hike**, not a casual stroll.\nThere are hills, uneven sections, and some ups and downs, so good walking or hiking shoes are important.\nPlease come prepared for typical fall weather and bring enough water for the hike.\n\nIf you're comfortable walking for a couple of hours and handling some elevation changes, you'll be fine.\nIf you're looking for something completely flat and easy, **this probably isn't the walk for you.**\n\n***\n\n## 🚌 Meetup Details\n\n### 🚇 By TTC\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** Don Mills Station — on the platform for the **85C bus**\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **9:45 AM**\n🚌 **Bus Leaves:** **10:06 AM sharp**\nI'll wait for the bus, but if you miss it, **you won't be able to join the group afterward.**\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n\n### 🚗 By Car\n\nParking is **not available at our TTC meeting point.**\n\nIf you're driving, please park at the **Toronto Zoo** and walk to the **Park's Welcome Centre (the house)**.\n🚗 **Car Meetup Time:** 11:00 AM\n\nWe may be a few minutes late arriving, depending on the bus and traffic.\n\n***\n\n## 🧺 The Picnic\n\nAfter the hike, we'll have a **30–40 minute group picnic** at the end.\nPlease bring something small to share — nothing too large or heavy. The goal is simply to have something to eat together after the hike.\n🥪 Sandwiches\n🍎 Fruit\n🍪 Snacks\n🥤 Drinks\nWhatever is easy to carry and share is perfect.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details at a Glance\n\n🥾 **Hike:** Approximately 2½ hours + short break\n🧺 **Picnic:** 30–40 minutes\n🏁 **End Point:** Park's Welcome Centre\n💲 **Meetup Fee:** $5 cash or e-transfer\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n🥾 Good walking shoes or hiking shoes\n🥪 A snack\n🧺 Something small to share for the picnic\n🧥 A fall jacket or layers\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis hike is great for:\n\n* People who enjoy a little challenge\n* Anyone who wants to explore Rouge National Urban Park\n* People who love fall colours 🍂\n* Hikers looking for a social outing\n* Anyone comfortable walking hills and uneven terrain\n* People who want to meet others while getting outside\n\nThis isn't the easiest walk we do.\n**But sometimes the harder walks are the ones you remember.**\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the hike.**\n**Stay for the picnic.**\n**Leave with a new connection — and maybe a new friend.** 🍂💛","startDate":"2026-10-24T13:45:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Don Mills Subway Station","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1800 Sheppard Avenue East,  M2J 5A7, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Wizards & Workouts - FREE","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-science-fiction-and-fantasy-writers-meetup/events/316670379/","description":"Do you consider rolling dice strength training?\nCan you run a D&D campaign, but not a city block?\nIf so, **WIZARDS & WORKOUTS** is for you.\n\nMy name is Peter Reynolds. I'm a writer and lover of role playing games. I'm also out of shape. I've been looking for ways to motivate myself to start working out with the same enthusiasm I bring to my Dungeons & Dragons campaign.\n\nThe plan is simple: host a fun, live role playing game where players take on the role of their favourite fantasy characters. The catch? You need to exercise if you want to succeed. Fighting a dragon? A fireball might cost you 5 pushups. Crossing a rooftop? Can you balance on one foot for a minute?\n\nBy combining simple, low impact exercises, including walking & stretching, with an interactive adventure, we'll all get healthier, have fun and maybe meet some new friends along the way. All fitness levels are welcome (as are dogs), and no previous knowledge of Dungeons & Dragons is necessary.\n\nWe meet in front of Broadview subway station at 10:00 am sharp and then walk to the Outdoor Fitness Station in Riverdale Park East (there are washrooms). At noon we start walking west, through the park, ending at the Blake House Restaurant \\* (Wellesley & Jarvis) by 12:30.\n\nAll sessions are free and I’ll be running them till it gets too cold. Hope to see you there!\n\n* The Blake House is where our Sci-Fi and Fantasy Writers' Group meets every Saturday from 1pm - 4pm to critique each other’s work. For more information on this event. Check out our Meetup events page.","startDate":"2026-10-24T14:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Broadview Subway Station","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Ontario","addressRegion":"on","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"769 Broadview Avenue, Ontario, on"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Science Fiction and Fantasy Writers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-science-fiction-and-fantasy-writers-meetup/"},"performer":"Toronto Science Fiction and Fantasy Writers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Brunch at Solena Brunch Bar - Saturday, October 24th, 2026 @11:00 AM","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-over-50-meetup-group/events/316743063/","description":"Hi Ladies,\nCome enjoy a delicious brunch with a Mediterranean twist on **Saturday**, October 24th, 2026 at **11:00 AM** at Solena Brunch Bar. The venue offers a wonderful variety of brunch options and beverage selections. Vegan choices are also available. The restaurant is bright and tastefully decorated with attentive waitstaff. The gratuity will be automatically added. Click [here](https://www.solenabrunch.ca/menu) for a link to the brunch menu. Meet friends and make some new ones while enjoying a lovely Brunch. Each participant will cover their own food and drink costs.\n**There is a non-refundable / non-transferable $5.00 cover fee** to attend this group event. This charge will reserve your spot, help with group costs and hopefully minimize no shows. **Payment of the $5 cover charge is due by FRIDAY, OCTOBER 16th, 2026.** After this date, non payment of the cover fee will result in the Member's name being